  {
   "text": "{\"sections\":[{\"section\":\"summary\",\"body\":\"On the bank's calculation, Brackmere Medical met all three covenants on the Venture Term Loan for the period ended October 31, 2026. The most important change is that the compliance certificate reports unrestricted cash and runway above the bank's figures: cash of {{fact:0ad7c62e-4233-4e2f-9ee6-a5ebc2b02114}} reported against {{fact:a280aeb3-37d8-4e61-b9b6-7bd220b149f0}} calculated, and runway of {{fact:43d05e00-fbae-478a-8e1a-47ed458a8f45}} against {{fact:ccb823a4-d9d6-4a9a-ad4e-4b352a725383}} months. Cushion on both liquidity covenants has narrowed over recent periods, with the largest drop in October. A high-severity open item on the cash mismatch needs a reviewer's resolution.\"},{\"section\":\"covenants\",\"body\":\"Minimum Unrestricted Cash is compliant at {{fact:a280aeb3-37d8-4e61-b9b6-7bd220b149f0}} against a {{fact:2e0970d5-4f5d-4491-bf43-4b2ff6fc2d2e}} floor, a cushion of {{fact:2906f61f-4b39-46a4-964a-c9a108fc19cf}}. The certificate reports a higher {{fact:0ad7c62e-4233-4e2f-9ee6-a5ebc2b02114}}. Minimum Runway is compliant at {{fact:ccb823a4-d9d6-4a9a-ad4e-4b352a725383}} months against a {{fact:b922f3af-45bc-42e7-abf0-39ee86c2a5e1}} month minimum, a cushion of {{fact:c088cb13-c166-4468-ba16-365e40e93a7c}}. The certificate reports a higher {{fact:43d05e00-fbae-478a-8e1a-47ed458a8f45}}. Revenue to Plan is compliant at {{fact:7afe03cb-986c-438b-a580-887f6533735b}} against an {{fact:5801d833-6a61-43d7-a541-8526ce1751ac}} floor, a cushion of {{fact:6bee3bb8-0aa3-4731-a413-f092a6711030}}. It matches the certificate. Both variances overstate liquidity, but neither changes the compliance outcome.\"},{\"section\":\"risks\",\"body\":\"The highest-priority item is the open, high-severity work item: bank statements and the certificate disagree on unrestricted cash. A reviewer should establish which cash figure is correct, since the runway variance likely follows from it. Next, unrestricted cash cushion has declined over consecutive periods and fell to {{fact:2906f61f-4b39-46a4-964a-c9a108fc19cf}} in October. Runway cushion followed the same path to {{fact:c088cb13-c166-4468-ba16-365e40e93a7c}}. The signals attribute this to faster cash burn or spending, but the bank does not hold burn or expense facts to confirm it. The revenue signal fired under the falling-headroom rule, although its own explanation describes revenue cushion as essentially flat.\"}]}",
   "type": "text"
  }
 ],
